# Admin build configuration. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# Compiled into the browser bundle and therefore public. Never put a credential
# in a `VITE_` variable.
#
# In the normal deployment the admin is built as part of the public site
# (`npm run build:all` from the parent directory), so it reads the PARENT's
# environment. This file matters when building or running the admin on its own.

# Origin of the API.
#
# Live backend (Render): https://majeed-portfolio-backend.onrender.com
#
# Leave it UNSET in local development — requests stay relative and Vite's dev
# proxy forwards them to localhost:8000, keeping everything same-origin.
#
# For production use https://api.<your-domain> rather than the raw onrender.com
# host. The session cookie is SameSite=Lax, which the browser sends only within
# one registrable domain: a site on `example.me` calling `api.example.me` works,
# a site on `*.vercel.app` calling `*.onrender.com` does not — login appears to
# succeed and every request after it is 401, and media thumbnails stay blank.
#
# It also feeds this app's Content-Security-Policy at build time: connect-src,
# img-src and frame-src are derived from it, so the policy cannot drift away
# from the API the build actually talks to.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
